<body>

    <main>

        <p><a href="../index.html">← Home</a></p>

        <h1>23/09/2026</h1>

        <p>
            Sometimes you’re so bored and horny you can’t do anything, nothing, whatsoever. Sometimes you are stuck in your bed and the sheets are oceans and mountains and the mattress is a cold and rocky floor and you are the largest you have ever been. Sometimes you are kind, sometimes you are not. This morning I woke up early with the sun. I was at Harvey’s house. For the past few weeks I have been nothing but tired, all the time. My head has felt light, almost dizzy, and my limbs are weak. I can hardly move. I’m fucking depressed. I need to get laid. Last night a beautiful woman complimented my jacket. I was flustered and coy and self-effacing and thought little of myself. I forgot almost entirely the strict code of conduct I had set myself, the way I was going to live from then on, the way that risk is important. ‘From here on out nothing changes’.
        </p>

        <p>
            My body is a ball of fast-twitching fibre that consumes air and confuses itself. I run away. Hardly a man.
        </p>

        <p>
            She was pretty. She had a green shirt that hung off her shoulder, revealing skin, revealing a rosebush strewn across her clavicle that slowly wound itself around her arm like smooth water. Her eyes danced and I felt the thrust of them towards me. I looked down. I didn’t say goodbye. I stared back towards her when I left the pub, but couldn’t find her, and I was walking too fast anyways.
        </p>

    </main>

</body>

</html>
